From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: captain <captain@lcars.local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:55:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Pinefeat CEF: don't take the rest of a stale line for the
 next reply

A reply that comes after its command's timeout (CEF_TIMEOUT) stays on
the line. sendCommand() flushed the input before each command and after
each reply, but tcflush() discards only what is already received: when
it cuts a late reply in two, the rest arrives after the flush and is
read as the reply to the next command, which takes it for its own (a
number for a position, an `ok` for an acknowledgement).

The input still pending before a command is now read and discarded
instead of flushed, which shows where it ends: if it ends inside a line,
the rest of that line is read up to its delimiter and discarded before
the reply. The input is no longer flushed after the reply: what follows
it is left to the next command, which discards it the same way. The
output is flushed before each command, as before.

This fixes the case of a late reply partly received when the next
command is sent. A late reply that arrives whole after the next command
was sent is still taken for its reply: the protocol carries nothing that
ties a reply to its command.

The cost: if the rest of a stale fragment never arrives (a controller
that stopped mid-line), the next command's reply is taken for that rest
and discarded, and the command fails after CEF_TIMEOUT, as when no reply
comes. The line is clean again for the command after it.
---
 drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp b/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp
index 5f9d01b..82baefb 100644
--- a/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp
+++ b/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp
@@ -24,9 +24,12 @@
 
 #include <connectionplugins/connectionserial.h>
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <cstring>
+#include <sys/ioctl.h>
 #include <termios.h>
 #include <thread>
+#include <unistd.h>
 
 #define ERR_NC(res) (strcmp(res, "nc") == 0 ? "lens is not attached" : res)
 
@@ -526,7 +529,20 @@ bool PinefeatCEF::sendCommand(const char * cmd, char * res)
 {
     int nbytes_written = 0, nbytes_read = 0, rc = -1;
 
-    tcflush(PortFD, TCIOFLUSH);
+    // The input still pending is stale (a reply that came after its command's timeout): it is read and discarded,
+    // as tcflush did, and if it ends inside a line, the rest of that line, still to come, is not this command's
+    // reply either
+    bool midLine = false;
+    int pending = 0;
+    while (ioctl(PortFD, FIONREAD, &pending) == 0 && pending > 0)
+    {
+        char stale[CEF_BUF];
+        ssize_t n = read(PortFD, stale, std::min(pending, int(sizeof(stale))));
+        if (n <= 0)
+            break;
+        midLine = stale[n - 1] != CEF_DEL;
+    }
+    tcflush(PortFD, TCOFLUSH);
 
     LOGF_DEBUG("CMD <%s>", cmd);
 
@@ -544,6 +560,19 @@ bool PinefeatCEF::sendCommand(const char * cmd, char * res)
         return true;
     }
 
+    char c = 0;
+    while (midLine)
+    {
+        if ((rc = tty_read(PortFD, &c, 1, CEF_TIMEOUT, &nbytes_read)) != TTY_OK)
+        {
+            char errstr[MAXRBUF] = {0};
+            tty_error_msg(rc, errstr, MAXRBUF);
+            LOGF_ERROR("Serial read error: %s.", errstr);
+            return false;
+        }
+        midLine = c != CEF_DEL;
+    }
+
     if ((rc = tty_nread_section(PortFD, res, CEF_BUF, CEF_DEL, CEF_TIMEOUT, &nbytes_read)) != TTY_OK)
     {
         char errstr[MAXRBUF] = {0};
@@ -559,7 +588,5 @@ bool PinefeatCEF::sendCommand(const char * cmd, char * res)
 
     LOGF_DEBUG("RES <%s>", res);
 
-    tcflush(PortFD, TCIOFLUSH);
-
     return true;
 }
